[
  "Shot with a Canon EOS R5, 85mm f/1.8 lens. The composition features two simple, round, matte-white ceramic bowls centered on an aged oak wood tabletop. The camera is at a 3/4 overhead angle to showcase the contents of both bowls, with one bowl sharp in the foreground and the second bowl slightly blurred in the background, creating a shallow depth of field. Soft, natural side light enters from a window on the left, casting gentle, elongated shadows and highlighting the creamy, pudding-like texture of the chia mixture. Each bowl is filled with a generous, thick, pearly-white chia and Greek yogurt pudding base, showing the tiny black specks of hydrated chia seeds. Scattered naturally on top of the pudding are plump, vibrant crimson raspberries and delicate, thin, toasted-beige sliced almonds. One bowl has a small, realistic smudge of yogurt on its inner rim. Beside the bowls, a worn linen napkin is rumpled casually, and a few stray fresh raspberries and almond slices are scattered on the wooden surface near a small stainless steel teaspoon. The atmosphere is warm, inviting, and cozy, with a golden-hour color palette. The scene looks like someone just finished prepping dessert at home, with slight, authentic imperfections: a small drop of maple syrup near the base of one bowl and uneven distribution of the fruit. Photorealistic, not AI-generated looking. The scene should look like someone just finished cooking and plating—lived-in, warm, authentic. No plastic sheen, no unnaturally smooth surfaces, no perfect symmetry. No text, no watermark, no logo, no hands, no faces. Indistinguishable from a photograph taken by a professional food photographer for a printed cookbook."
]
